# VS Code Cheatsheet — HTML / CSS / JS / TS

Default **Windows/Linux** keybindings. Since you're on Linux/Ubuntu, these should be the most relevant.

---

## 1. ⭐ The 15 shortcuts worth memorizing

| Shortcut              | Action                |
| --------------------- | --------------------- |
| `Ctrl + Shift + P`    | Command Palette       |
| `Ctrl + P`            | Quick Open file       |
| `Ctrl + Shift + F`    | Search entire project |
| `Ctrl + F`            | Find in current file  |
| `Ctrl + H`            | Replace               |
| `Ctrl + Space`        | Trigger autocomplete  |
| `Ctrl + .`            | Quick Fix             |
| `F12`                 | Go to Definition      |
| `Shift + F12`         | Find References       |
| `Alt + F12`           | Peek Definition       |
| `F2`                  | Rename Symbol         |
| `Shift + Alt + F`     | Format Document       |
| `Ctrl + /`            | Toggle comment        |
| `Alt + ↑ / ↓`         | Move line             |
| `Shift + Alt + ↑ / ↓` | Duplicate line        |

If you learn only these initially, you'll already be very productive.

